This plugin vendors three skills from Matt Pocock's "Skills for Real Engineers":

    https://github.com/mattpocock/skills

    skills/engineering/grill-with-docs   -> skills/grill-with-docs
    skills/productivity/grilling         -> skills/grilling
    skills/engineering/domain-modeling   -> skills/domain-modeling

Upstream commit:

    5b15a47f2d7150f545fbcacbfe381787fc0230dc

Only these three are vendored: `grill-with-docs` is a thin wrapper that runs
`/grilling` using the `/domain-modeling` skill, so the three form the minimal
closure. Upstream ships 36 skills; the rest are deliberately not carried here.

LOCAL MODIFICATIONS
-------------------

These files are NOT verbatim. Four patches apply on top of upstream, in order:

    patches/0001-lowercase-doc-filenames.patch
    patches/0002-conditional-round-delivery.patch
    patches/0003-drop-context-map.patch
    patches/0004-enable-model-invocation.patch

0001 lowercases the doc-artifact name this repo standardises on - CONTEXT.md ->
context.md - and renames the skill's own reference docs to match (ADR-FORMAT.md ->
adr-format.md, CONTEXT-FORMAT.md -> context-format.md). On a case-sensitive filesystem
the uppercase names would be separate, competing files, so this is a correctness fix
rather than a cosmetic one. It touches `domain-modeling` only. CONTEXT-MAP.md keeps its
uppercase name here, because 0003 deletes every line that names it and renaming a doomed
line only makes the two patches fight.

0002 changes how `grilling` delivers a round and how `grill-with-docs` composes, not how
either one thinks. Upstream asks the whole frontier as a numbered prose block with emoji
headers, which leaves the user writing an essay to answer it. A round now goes through the
AskUserQuestion tool when that tool is in the model's list: up to 4 questions per call, 2-4
selectable options each, the recommendation first. Codex has no AskUserQuestion and no
Skill tool, so the same text says what to do without them - ask one question per turn with
up to 4 numbered options and end the turn, which keeps the round-per-turn rhythm and still
avoids the numbered essay this patch exists to prevent. Upstream's design-tree and frontier
model is kept intact. The check is inline in the vendored text because a model can read its
own tool list. The same patch gives `grill-with-docs`'s one-line body a second sentence:
without a Skill tool, read `../grilling/SKILL.md` and `../domain-modeling/SKILL.md` and
follow both. Those paths are relative to the file that names them, which is why they climb
a level. Its last hunk flips `allow_implicit_invocation` in
`grill-with-docs/agents/openai.yaml` from false to true, which is the Codex half of the
decision 0004 makes on the Claude side; upstream ships that flag paired with the
`disable-model-invocation: true` that 0004 removes.

0003 removes the `context-map.md` mechanism from `domain-modeling`: the multi-context
directory tree in SKILL.md, and the map file plus the structure-inference list in
context-format.md. We do not use a map file; the `## Contexts` section of a repo's
AGENTS.md is the map. Note what it deliberately does NOT do. It does not assert that a
repo is single-context, because flow's prep stage forbids inferring that from a missing
map file, and it keeps "when multiple contexts exist, infer which one the topic relates
to", which still applies when the map lives elsewhere. It also rewords SKILL.md's
"Most repos have a single context" lead-in - the surviving half of a deleted contrast -
to stay neutral about context count. The blocks it deletes carry `context.md` in the
spelling 0001 gave them, so it applies after 0001 and nowhere else.

0004 drops `disable-model-invocation: true` from `grill-with-docs`'s frontmatter, so the
model can invoke the skill itself instead of waiting for the user to type the slash
command. It touches that one file's frontmatter, and the body line it carries as context
is the sentence 0002 wrote, so it applies after 0002. SKILL.md keeps its uppercase name -
the skill loader discovers skills by that exact filename.

RE-SYNCING
----------

    1. Copy the three upstream directories over skills/
    2. git apply patches/0001-lowercase-doc-filenames.patch
    3. git apply patches/0002-conditional-round-delivery.patch
    4. git apply patches/0003-drop-context-map.patch
    5. git apply patches/0004-enable-model-invocation.patch
    6. Update the commit SHA above; regenerate any patch that stops applying

The patches are ordinary `git diff` output with `a/plugins/grill/skills/...` paths, so
apply them from the repo root. To regenerate one: commit the state it applies to, redo the
change on top of that, and `git diff -M` the two commits. Verify the whole chain by
applying it to a fresh copy of upstream in a scratch directory and diffing the result
against skills/. They must be byte-identical.

